{"name":"Limoges","hex":"#243f6c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Limoges","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city, the capital of Haute-Vienne department, Nouvelle-Aquitaine, France, formerly the capital of the old Limousin region."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Limoges"}],"entries":[{"title":"Limoges","blocks":[{"text":"Limoges is a city and commune, and the prefecture of the Haute-Vienne department in west-central France. It was the administrative capital of the former Limousin region. Situated on the first western foothills of the Massif Central, Limoges is crossed by the river Vienne, of which it was originally the first ford crossing point."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Centre-ville_et_champ_de_Juillet.JPG/330px-Centre-ville_et_champ_de_Juillet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limoges","wikidata":"Q45656"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Limoges_Mairie.jpg/500px-Limoges_Mairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Limoges_Mairie.jpg/1280px-Limoges_Mairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Limoges_Mairie.jpg/500px-Limoges_Mairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALimoges_Mairie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Limoges_st_michel_lions_2_%2822378242672%29.jpg/500px-Limoges_st_michel_lions_2_%2822378242672%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Limoges_st_michel_lions_2_%2822378242672%29.jpg/1280px-Limoges_st_mi